    1. Pick grid dimensions H in [4,6], W in [4,6]
    2. Choose 5 distinct colors from {0..9} excluding orange (7)
    3. Assign target counts for each color such that the top 2 are strictly above the remaining 3, with no tie at the 2nd/3rd boundary; ensure counts sum to H*W
    4. Fill grid by randomly shuffling a flat array of (count_i copies of color_i), then reshape to (H, W)
    5. Compute output by replacing all non-top-2 pixels with orange (7)
