    single column of uniform non-bg color spanning full grid height
    separates sprite strip from frame
  frame:
    base_color: single non-bg color (≠ divider, ≠ any sprite color)
    rectangle spanning full grid height; width = interior_w + 2
    edges: top==bottom mirrored, left==right mirrored
    markers: mover colors placed at matching positions on both opposite edges
    interior: 8-13 rows × 8-13 cols, filled with bg
    extra non-matching colors on edges [observed]
  sprites:
    count: 2-3 movers + 0-1 distractors = 2-4 total
    shape: 8-connected single-color blob, 3-9 pixels, bbox 1-5 × 1-5
    colors: all distinct, ≠ bg, ≠ frame_base, ≠ divider
    placed in left strip (cols 0..divider-1), no mutual overlap
    movers: color has matching markers on both L/R and T/B frame edges
    distractors: color absent from frame edge markers; unchanged in output
  markers:
    per mover: 1-2 row marks × 1-2 col marks
    row mark: both L and R frame edges have mover's color at that row
    col mark: both T and B frame edges have mover's color at that col
    no two movers share a row mark or col mark
  transformation:
    erase movers from left strip
    stamp each mover centered at Cartesian product of row_marks × col_marks
